{"type":"message","id":"f4636658","parentId":"866d0a49","timestamp":"2026-05-29T10:46:00.601Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API endpoints are not responding well. The root and /api return \"Unauthorized\", and /send returns error 1101. But the GET /history endpoints work fine with the same API key header. This suggests the POST /send endpoint might have a different issue.\n\nError 1101 might be a custom error code meaning something like \"invalid request\" or \"thread not found\" or similar. The API key auth works for GET but POST fails. Could be that the POST endpoint expects a different field name.\n\nLet me try with `text` instead of `content`, or see if there's a different endpoint structure.\n\nActually, I notice the history endpoint uses query parameters not path parameters. Maybe /send also uses query parameters? Let me try:\n\n\ncurl -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration\" with just a simple body","thinkingSignature":"4a2a6272dbcca205cafe9f001fcdf838e32ebd2b938db247e59e22448dab8e08"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ubuz8tfd4q5c_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try different body format\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -d '{\"text\":\"heartbeat test\"}'"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ubuz8tfd4q5c_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration&content=heartbeat_test\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" 2>&1"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":35,"output":350,"cacheRead":22272,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22657,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780051554179,"responseId":"0668a162784412829c13