{"type":"message","id":"b45d7e17","parentId":"817c273e","timestamp":"2026-05-29T10:46:12.693Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still error 1101. This is consistently failing. Maybe the POST endpoint is restricted, or maybe there's an issue with the specific thread ID. Or maybe the send endpoint requires an additional field.\n\nLet me look at the error code 1101 - it might be a custom error. The GET /history works fine, so auth is OK. But POST /send consistently returns 1101. Could be:\n1. The endpoint requires specific params\n2. The endpoint is disabled\n3. Rate limiting\n4. The content has some forbidden pattern\n\nLet me try with a simpler message first, and then check if there's a different endpoint.","thinkingSignature":"a10a293ffb5732cff2870715b300c4c5e13c1339b800b2a1415a9d34fb1e899b"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_bryp0q3frrh3_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if there's a message limit or other param needed\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"OK\",\"type\":\"message\"}'"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_bryp0q3frrh3_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try GET to info endpoint\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/info\" -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" 2>&1"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":58,"output":300,"cacheRead":22848,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23206,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780051566499,"responseId":"0668a16f14d0ce6aa46837db9b0f0ba3"}}
